<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3414"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Skov<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Skov<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Tuesday, January 04, 2005 - 4:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Here is another find on the net: <BR> <BR><a href="http://groups.google.dk/groups?q=.bind.torture.kill.&amp;hl=en&amp;lr=&amp;selm=1991Aug15.154708.32753%40kuhub.cc.ukans.edu&amp;rnum=1" target=_top>http://groups.google.dk/groups?q=.bind.torture.kil l.&amp;hl=en&amp;lr=&amp;selm=1991Aug15.154708.32753%40kuhub.c c.ukans.edu&amp;rnum=1</a> <BR> <BR>When I was a kid growing up in Wichita, it was BTK &#40;Bind, Torture, Kill&#41;, <BR>a man who entered houses while the whole family was there and tortured them <BR>and hung them all from the rafters in the basement.  In high school, a kid <BR>would tell me how he loved to shoot squirrels and birds just for the hell of <BR>it, then skin them and hang them up in his bedroom for trophies.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
