<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7226"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 7:30 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The book by Judy Chard called &#34;person unknown&#34; was originally published in 1988, and is a romance novel. This Patricia Gragg site has only been up a year or two. I think Chard is also from the UK. <BR>Patricia Gragg apparently edited this for somebody, I would like to know who the writer was. <BR>Also strange is the fact that Gragg says she authored 2 books, but when you look at the books covers they have a different authors name. Could be a psuedonym I guess.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
