<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7235"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:bmodule_244@hotmail.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Bmodule<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bmodule<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 9:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I&#39;m thinking there is more than one book titled &#39;Person Unknown&#39;. Perhaps googling on the wrong side of the road will help. I&#39;ll give it a shot.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7235-->
<!--Post: 7272--><!--Time: 1108346614-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7272"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ztargate<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ztargate<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 13, 2005 - 6:03 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->That story is another example of great literary talent wasted on accounts of senseless violent crimes against women, passed on as somewhat erotic and worthy of a reader&#39;s time. <BR> <BR>I read up until the moment he attacked the woman, and I had to stop reading. Not because the story was shocking or scary, but because the story&#39;s tone was making the attack more of a love-making erotic kind of tale, rather than a horrible violent criminal attack against a woman. <BR> <BR>It is because of people like the author and those who publish their work, that some men get caught up in the lust and the fantasy of the storyline and then they go out and hurt women themselves. <BR> <BR>Pure literary trash, I would say. <BR> <BR>------------ <BR> <BR>Thanks for the link. I know that if we are discussing violent criminals like BTK this type of violence against women has to be referenced, and the link does have references to BTK and his attacks.  <BR> <BR>I just hope and pray that no other man gets &#34;inspired&#34; by the BTK case and starts his own serial killing spree of his own.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7272-->
<!--Post: 7306--><!--Time: 1108392289-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7306"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, February 14, 2005 - 6:44 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;KAKE-TV showed film footage of the contents of a package, including an unidentified wrapped metallic object and blurred images of three pages purported to be a list of chapters of a book entitled &#34;The BTK Story.&#34;&#34; <BR> <BR>Thats the first time I read &#34;unidentified metallic object. <BR> <BR>In the story referenced above, the killer takes a metal decorative cigarette lighter or cigarette case. Just one more coincidence.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
