<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7817"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, February 17, 2005 - 5:56 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Excerpt about letter rec&#39;d by Kake in 2004 <BR> <BR>The KAKE letter contained three pages, including photocopied identifications of &#34;Special Officer&#34; from Southwestern Bell and the Wichita school district. Both SBC and the school district said employees don&#39;t show up at homes unannounced.  <BR> <BR>: The copy of the school ID badge contained a logo not used by Wichita public schools until 1988, district spokeswoman Susan Arensman said. She said officials found it on only one document prior to 1986.  <BR><a href="http://forum.creeindian.com/_disc1/0000024e.htm" target=_top>http://forum.creeindian.com/_disc1/0000024e.htm</a> <BR> <BR>That puts a date on the school id badge, after 1988. There is some more info in this article that I haven&#39;t read before. <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
